Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||04-06-2000||05:48 PM||||I usually remember all my dreams, unless I'm woken up by the phone ringing, etc and I start thinking about other things before I have time to remember the dreams.<P>Anyway, I've been studying dreams for about a year now, and I have several books on dream symbolism. Often if I have a particularly vivid dream, I'll look up the symbols in the dream.. usually when I do this, I look up the symbols in all the dreams I can remember from that night. and most of the time, the symbols all carry a similar message..<BR>The images themselves are usually created out of things you've been thinking about, so if you see a car in a dream, it might be one you've seen recently, or been thinking about.. not always tho. This tends to happen more often with people, a person you know might be in a dream but they're just representing something/someone else.<BR>This is also the case with locations/situations.<BR>for example, I seem to have a lot of dreams about school.. Often there are high school teachers there, but the school is never the high school. it's always the elementary school I went to. It seems that this particular building/location is what my subconscious pictures as "school", so that's always how a school appears in my dreams.<P>A lot of people I know don't think dreams mean anything, that they're the product of something you saw on tv, or a reaction from something you ate.. but a large number of your dreams are symbolic messages from your subconscious, and you can gain insight into your own subconscious by recording and interpreting your dreams. If the dreams are ridiculously weird, such as people with purple skin, or something totally impossible like that, then there's a good chance it is caused by food, or a tv show, etc. If not, pay attention. it could be important.<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 04-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||04-06-2000||08:34 PM||||That's a funny kid.  GT Bastard, did you have to fill in any blanks?  That was some funny sh!t.  Can I claim that as my dream and tell it to my friends?  Anyone remember the movie "Tremors" with Kevin Bacon?  I think it was made in the late 80s early 90s.  Anyway, I had a dream when I was five years old (that was in 1984) where these giant blue worms were terrorizing my neighborhood.  They were popping out of storm sewers and such and chomping on people.  With a few exceptions, the dream was pretty much based around the movie or should I say the movie was based around the dream.  The dream didn't so much freak me out as the movie did.  I mean the shape and everthing about the worms in the movie was similar to the dream, only the worms were brown.  And it was one of those repeating dreams so I really got a chance to remeber the details.  Do you remember when the worm was tricked into falling off that cliff at the end of the movie?  That was cool.||||reg||11
